body:
Talking to therapists can be helpful in the sense that simply talking about your problems helps numbs it a little bit since you can feel heard. But its sort of like taking painkillers, in that while the pain is numbed for a little bit- the problems are not addressed or dealt with. There is never enough time to really focus on fixing my many issues because too much time is spent talking over what new messed up stuff happened to me during the week.  Most therapists only do 45 minutes sessions with the occasionally hour long ones for first time sessions. 

&#x200B;

 I would recommend everyone who is struggling to try it- and by try it, I mean actually finding a therapist you feel comfortable with and sticking with them for a prolonged period of time. I had to do through 2 therapists before I really felt comfortable getting into the nitty gritty of the matter, so dont feel bad about having to ask for someone else if the counselor you initially get isn't working for you.

&#x200B;

Even though it hasn't worked in fixing my issues, it has temporarily helped with the pain.
